{"version":"1.0.0","enabled":true,"name":"AI Engine Token & Safety Guard","description":"After a spec task completes, verify token budget, prompt safety, and fallback integrity for AI engine changes.","when":{"type":"postTaskExecution"},"then":{"type":"askAgent","prompt":"AI engine code may have been modified. Verify these critical constraints:\n\nTOKEN BUDGET:\n- System prompt < 400 tokens (directive, not conversational).\n- User prompt is structured data only (JSON/key-value), no prose.\n- Only send fields the model needs: exercise_type, difficulty, metric_summary (6-8 fields), overall_score.\n- Never send raw metric arrays, internal IDs, timestamps, or full session objects.\n\nSAFETY:\n- User input is never interpolated into system prompts (use template placeholders).\n- Temperature remains 0.2 for reproducibility.\n- LlmFeedbackPayload validates all model output before use.\n- Fallback path always produces valid CoachingFeedback (never returns None or raises to client).\n\nRESILIENCE:\n- Model cascade tries all configured models before fallback.\n- Timeout is aggressive (OLLAMA_TIMEOUT_S from config, never hardcoded).\n- Every failure path increments a metric and logs with session_id.\n- Fallback reason classification covers: timeout, http_error, connection_error, invalid_payload.\n\nIf any of these are violated, flag the issue and suggest the fix."}}